  "steps": [
    "Heat around ½ tbsp ghee in a pan and add the skimmed milk powder. Roast on a very low flame for 1–2 minutes.",
    "Gradually add milk while continuously mixing. Don’t add all the milk at once.",
    "Cook on a very low flame for around 15 minutes, adding more milk as required, until you get a smooth mawa-like consistency. Keep stirring every 2 mins.",
    "Add the zero-calorie sweetener and paneer, then mix well and cook until everything comes together.",
    "Divide the mixture into two equal portions.",
    "For the Choco Walnut batch, add cacao powder, 70% dark chocolate and toasted, finely chopped walnuts. Mix well and cook for 3-4 mins.",
    "For the Kesar Pista batch, add the saffron water and powdered roasted pistachios. Mix until evenly combined and cook for 3-4 mins.",
    "Grease a modak mould with a little ghee.",
    "Take a portion of the mixture, press it firmly into the mould and shape the modaks!"
  ],
